    "title": "Central repo manifest enables fleet-wide updates via `diwa update`",
    "body": "To let a single `diwa update` command propagate improved hook scripts, extraction prompts, and reflection criteria to every repo a user has set up, diwa needed a persistent registry of which repos are managed. `diwa init` now writes an entry to ~/.diwa/repos.json and `diwa uninit` removes it, making the manifest the source of truth for which repos to upgrade/reindex. This decouples 'improving diwa' from 'manually re-running setup in every repo', solving the problem of stale hooks/prompts across multiple projects.",
