    "category": "architecture",
    "title": "Services tab bridges local process discovery with Cloudflare tunnel state",
    "body": "Instead of maintaining a separate manual mapping of services to tunnels, the app scans actual listening ports via lsof and resolves project identity from process working directories, then cross-references this against live Cloudflare ingress rules fetched via the API. This gives a real-time, ground-truth view of what's running locally versus what's actually exposed through a tunnel, rather than relying on static config. Credentials for the CF API call are extracted directly from the existing cert.pem rather than requiring separate API token configuration.",
